# Root-level environment reference for BountyFlow Pro.
#
# This project actually uses environment variables in TWO separate places
# with two separate files — do not merge them:
#
#   1. frontend/.env.local       — consumed by Next.js at build/runtime.
#                                   Auto-generated by scripts/configure-frontend.ps1
#                                   after a deployment. See frontend/.env.local.example
#                                   for the exact variable names.
#
#   2. GitHub Actions secrets    — used only by .github/workflows/deploy-contracts.yml
#                                   to deploy contracts from CI. Configure under
#                                   Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions:
#                                     DEPLOYER_SECRET_KEY   (Stellar secret key, testnet only)
#
#   3. Vercel project settings   — the frontend's production environment variables
#                                   (same names as frontend/.env.local.example) are
#                                   set directly in the Vercel dashboard, not committed.
#
# This root .env.example exists only to document that separation. There is
# no root-level .env consumed directly by any part of this project.
